Let $T$ be the oriented left-handed trefoil, the closure of the two-strand braid $\sigma_1^{-3}$, and choose a marked point away from its three crossings. Its mirror $\overline T$ is the closure of $\sigma_1^3$, depicted below. Use the smoothing convention in which the zero-resolution of this mirror diagram is the through pairing and the one-resolution is the cap-cup pairing. The reduced Khovanov cohomology of $\overline T$ over $\mathbb F_2$ has total rank $3$. The double branched cover of $T$ is a lens space $L(3,1)$ up to orientation, and the hat Floer group of this lens space over $\mathbb F_2$ has total rank $3$. Thus the $E_2$ page and the abutment have equal total rank. Every spectral-sequence differential $d_r$ with $r\ge2$ vanishes; the rank comparison gives no conclusion about the earlier differential $d_1$ from $E_1$ to $E_2$.

~~~tikz
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.55]
\draw (-1,6) .. controls (-3,6) and (-3,0) .. (-1,0);
\draw (1,6) .. controls (3,6) and (3,0) .. (1,0);
\foreach \yt/\yb in {6/4,4/2,2/0} {
  \draw (-1,\yt) -- (1,\yb);
  \draw[white,line width=4pt] (1,\yt) -- (-1,\yb);
  \draw[black,line width=1.1pt] (1,\yt) -- (-1,\yb);
}
\node at (0,7) {$\widehat{\sigma_1^3}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
~~~

The drawing depicts the closure of the braid word; the southwest-to-northeast diagonal is drawn over the northwest-to-southeast diagonal, matching the positive-generator convention in the rank calculation. The algebraic calculation uses the smoothing cube and Frobenius maps, not the picture.

